================ REAL-DATA QUALITY OBSERVATIONS ================
  AP by year: [{"year":2022,"ap":121894},{"year":2023,"ap":93591},{"year":2024,"ap":722}]
  [FINDING RC-05 P1] Real extraction produced an implausible AP for FY2024 and the engine computes on it without complaint :: fsl-bs-ap FY2024 = 722 tys. PLN vs FY2023 = 93591 and FY2022 = 121894. A >99% one-year collapse in trade payables for a group with PLN 1.23bn revenue is an extraction defect, not a business event. No readiness check, reconciliation rule or KPI quality flag catches it — DPO is computed and stored as a normal value.
  FY2022 P0 codes NOT directly extracted (7): EBITDA, DEPRECIATION, TAX_EXPENSE, NET_INCOME, WORKING_CAPITAL, CFO, FCF
  FY2023 P0 codes NOT directly extracted (9): EBITDA, DEPRECIATION, TAX_EXPENSE, NET_INCOME, AR, WORKING_CAPITAL, CFO, CFF, FCF
  FY2024 P0 codes NOT directly extracted (6): EBITDA, DEPRECIATION, NET_INCOME, WORKING_CAPITAL, CFO, FCF
  AR by year: [{"year":2022,"ar":189804},{"year":2023,"ar":null},{"year":2024,"ar":185495}]
  [FINDING RC-06 P2] A required KPI input is missing for one year only, silently degrading two KPIs :: fsl-bs-ar is extracted for FY2022 (189804) and FY2024 (185495) but NOT for FY2023 — the same statement type from the same issuer, one year apart. Average-balance DSO and CASH_CONVERSION_CYCLE for FY2024 therefore cannot be computed. This is an extractor coverage gap, and its downstream effect is visible only as a MISSING KPI status.